window.products.push({"id":88024,"name":"Pour over Coffee Filter – Food Grade Stainless Steel Reusable Coffee Filter by HILL – Paperless–Single Cup Coffee Dripper - Barista Grade Pour-Over Fi","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/911HOzUXaZS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Coffee ground selection If your coffee grounds are too coarse, it tends to under-extract (souracidic). If your grounds are too fine, you tend to over-extract (bitteroverpowering). Our recommendation will be to use MediumMedium coarse grounds. The designed300Mesh is perfect for this combination. It ensures a good drip ratio and prevents filter clog. As individual’s taste and preference differ, do adjust accordingly until you find your own sweet spot. How to use Pour over coffee brew is fast catching up to be popular among coffee enthusiasts. Apart from the exceptional flavor, the process greatly enhanced the experience for the brewerdrinker. For some, the pouring is meditative and calming. It almost puts you in a state of zen, helping you to a good start to the morning (or slows you down from a hectic day). The other important parameters are the coffee-water ratio, water quality and water temperature. And of course, you need – HILL’s Pour Over Coffee Filter to complete the process. The coffee to water ratio is typically 1:16. We recommend 21g of coffee to 335g of water for a single cup brew. Good quality water is a must and the recommended temperature is about 195-205degF (90 - 96degC). Fill Coffee Filter with grounded coffee and tap the edges gently to even the pile. The initial short stage of the brew, commonly known as “Bloom” is important for even extraction. Pour a small amount enough to cover the grounds. It will allow the water to saturate the grounds and initiate a period of degassing. This should take 30seconds and we estimate21g of coffee will need about 40g(40ml) of water to bloom evenly. Once the “Bloom” phase is over, you can proceed to brew. Even pouring is crucial to even extraction. Pour slowly and in circular motions to ensure the grounds are being impacted with the same amount of water. p","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/911HOzUXaZS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Hill","source_asin":"B093TF93D4","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-88024","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B093TF93D4","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B093TF93D4","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
